## 🔍 Dataset Description
- **Source**: Publicly available Canadian income data
- **Features**:
  - `Year`
  - `Average Income`
- The dataset represents the **average annual income of Canadian citizens over multiple years**.

---

## ⚙️ Methodology
1. Load and preprocess the dataset
2. Visualize income trends over time
3. Define the Linear Regression hypothesis
4. Implement the cost function (MSE)
5. Optimize parameters using Gradient Descent
6. Train the model on historical data
7. Generate predictions
8. Visualize regression line and model fit

---

## 📊 Results & Observations
- The model successfully captures the **upward trend** in average income over time
- Gradient descent converges smoothly with an appropriate learning rate
- The regression line closely fits the data, demonstrating the effectiveness of linear modeling for trend analysis

